@1 = ~Quest for Ingredients requires Baldur's Gate: Enhanced Edition Trilogy (EET).~
@2 = ~Required vanilla resource MISC97.ITM was not found.~
@3 = ~Required vanilla resource MISCAZ.ITM was not found.~
@100 = ~Quentin's Components~
@101 = ~Quentin's Components

Quentin has asked us to find nine rare ingredients for his Potion of Tomorrow. He has promised 200 gold coins for each component we deliver.~
@102 = ~Quentin's Components

Blood Wyvern's Venom has been delivered to Quentin.~
@103 = ~Quentin's Components

Ripplebark has been delivered to Quentin.~
@104 = ~Quentin's Components

Spider Poison has been delivered to Quentin.~
@105 = ~Quentin's Components

Dragonspear Wine has been delivered to Quentin.~
@106 = ~Quentin's Components

Duergar Brandy has been delivered to Quentin.~
@107 = ~Quentin's Components

Luriyl Gem has been delivered to Quentin.~
@108 = ~Quentin's Components

The Eye of the Ancient Beholder has been delivered to Quentin.~
@109 = ~Quentin's Components

The Golden Rose has been delivered to Quentin.~
@110 = ~Quentin's Components

The Tarrasque Claw has been delivered to Quentin.~
@111 = ~Quentin's Components

Quentin revealed his true intentions. He sought to become a lich and use the completed elixir to bring death and destruction to the Sword Coast. He was slain before he could carry out his plan.~
@201 = ~A handwritten list of the ingredients Quentin needs for his Potion of Tomorrow.

Blood Wyvern's Venom - likely Cloakwood
Ripplebark - unknown
Spider Poison - likely Cloakwood
Dragonspear Wine - Dragonspear Castle
Duergar Brandy - unknown
Luriyl Gem - unknown
Eye of the Ancient Beholder - they are rare to find
Golden Rose - Oberan's Estate
Tarrasque Claw - Tomb in Amkethran

Quentin has noted that some of these components may be extremely dangerous to obtain. He claims to know where some of them can be found, but not all.~
@202 = ~What am I supposed to do now? This is awful... just awful.~
@203 = ~Hey. Are you all right?~
@204 = ~Cease your lamenting. We don't need to hear it.~
@205 = ~Eh, no. I'm not all right. My name is Quentin of New Sharandar. An illustrious alchemist, and well on my way to becoming a well-known one. I studied potions and herbs all my life, and all I want is to elevate myself, but it is a tumultuous road.~
@206 = ~I travelled all this way to Beregost to find a few ingredients that I need to create a very unique potion. Potion of Tomorrow. Yeah, yeah, I know—the name needs some polish. But what is important is that I possibly possess the knowledge on how to make it come true. Alas, I am missing a few crucial components. What's worse, locating them has proven a far heftier task than I ever anticipated.~
@207 = ~On my list I have Blood Wyvern's Venom, Ripplebark, Spider Poison, Dragonspear Wine, Duergar Brandy, Luriyl Gem, Eye of the Ancient Beholder, Golden Rose and Tarrasque Claw. Collecting some of these is... lethal in nature, to put it lightly. I fear gathering such components poses a bigger threat to me than I thought.~
@208 = ~What if we look for these components during our travels?~
@209 = ~We are adventurers but... I don't think I know where to find such items.~
@210 = ~We are sorry, but we don't have time to look for such things. No offence.~
@211 = ~You would? That would mean a world to me. If you ever encounter any of these, make sure to promptly report back to me. I do have some gold at my disposal, so for each component I offer you... 200 gold coins. And if you bring me all of them, I'll give you a reward for it. Something more valuable to adventurers of your sort than mere gold.~
@212 = ~Not to worry. I have devised a list that specifies places in which said components are likely to be found. Well, some of them. A minority I sadly have no clue where to look for. But as long as you traverse the whole region and keep an eye out, I'm sure at least a few can be located.~
@213 = ~I do have some gold at my disposal, so for each component I offer you... 200 gold coins. And if you bring me all of them, I'll give you a reward for it. Something more valuable to adventurers of your sort than mere gold.~
@214 = ~Here. Take this list. I wrote down everything you need to know. If you ever lose it, come back to me and I can write you another one. Good luck on your travels, and please keep an eye out.~
@215 = ~No offence taken. I am aware of the perils that go with this request. You owe me no apology. I shall find other brave souls. Farewell.~
@216 = ~Is there anything else you need?~
@217 = ~We changed our minds. We want to work for you.~
@218 = ~No. Just checking in.~
@219 = ~Wait, that's... all the components. You really did it! After all that time, you really did it! I am forever in your debt, my friend. You saved me so much personal effort.~
@220 = ~ ~
@221 = ~We found Blood Wyvern's Venom.~
@222 = ~We found Ripplebark.~
@223 = ~We found Spider Poison.~
@224 = ~We found Dragonspear Wine.~
@225 = ~We found Duergar Brandy.~
@226 = ~We found a Luriyl Gem.~
@227 = ~We found the Eye of the Ancient Beholder.~
@228 = ~We found the Golden Rose.~
@229 = ~We found the Tarrasque Claw.~
@230 = ~Still searching.~
@231 = ~We lost the list. Can you write us another copy?~
@232 = ~Terrific. Here are 200 gold coins. If you find any more, bring them to me.~
@233 = ~Go on then. Don't keep me waiting.~
@234 = ~Now, becoming a lich shouldn't be difficult. The elixir I shall make will amplify my powers, and I can finally wipe this land from the earth and make it a cold, gloomy place filled with death and destruction.~
@235 = ~What?!~
@236 = ~Do not worry that little head of yours. I shall spare you that fate. Friend to a friend, leave these lands and do not come back, lest you wish to perish alongside all the others. The Sword Coast has been decaying with greed, apathy, banditry and bigotry for so long. Once its inhabitants are no more, corruption will be gone too.~
@237 = ~As my father once taught me, "you live only once, unless you truly wish to remain alive forever." And I shall chase that dream and become a...~
@238 = ~(slit his throat as he talks)~
@239 = ~Enough of this. I won't let you get away.~
@240 = ~(With a swift swing of your blade, you slit Quentin's throat, abruptly ending the puny elf's monologue. Red liquid pours down his chest as he grabs his own throat in sheer surprise. He falls to his knees and sends you one last look before collapsing to the floor. Even in death, his gaze seems fixed upon you. His dreams of lichdom have gone to oblivion. An ugly feeling of anger creeps in. How could you have fallen into this wicked elf's trap?)~
@241 = ~There's nothing you can do to stop me.~
@242 = ~(slit his throat)~
@243 = ~You can't stop me. I am already on my way to lichdom, and soon the whole of Toril will tremble at the mere mention of my name. I will ascend to godhood and take over Kelemvor's position.~
